After the biosynthetic stage the product goes through **downstream processing**:
- first it is **separated** from the culture and then **purified** (separation and purification);
- the purified product is then **formulated with suitable preservatives**;
- a drug or similar product must then go through thorough **clinical trials** (and strict quality control) before it is ready for marketing.

So the sequence is separation, purification, formulation, clinical trial. So the answer is option (C) (iii) \(\rightarrow\) (i) \(\rightarrow\) (ii) \(\rightarrow\) (iv).
